                        {
                          "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                          "Text": "The \"a\" multiplier fixes the rate of leaf appearance on a \"shoot\" basis. Eventually each shoot will have ~15 leaves.\n\n#leaves/shoot = 15\n\n#shoots = 12\n\n#canes = 24\n\nVineArea = 24 m2\n\n\nleaves/m2 = (24 * 12 * 15)/24 = 180\n\n\n180 leaves/m2 is within an acceptable range based on the following reference:\n\n\nE f f e c t s of Partial D e f o l i a t i o n at Various S t a g e s of\nthe G r o w i n g S e a s o n on Fruit Yields, Root G r o w t h\nand R e t u r n B l o o m of K i w i f r u i t V i n e s (1990), Buwalda & Smith, Fig.2(a) ==> (FZ + RCZ to account for both the \"Fruit Zone\" and \"Replaced Cane Zone\")",
